WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.210
Is one third the same as 3 ninths?

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:06.760
Split each third into three equal parts.

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:09.960
Top and bottom were both multiplied by 3.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:15.840
So one third equals 3 ninths. Same amount, new name.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:21.013
That works for any number, as long as top and bottom match.
